{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/144079-sea-wolves","id":144079,"title":"\"Sea Wolves\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-20T21:09:13-07:00","id":144079,"title":"\"Sea Wolves\"","content":"I'm interested, as this thing stucked to my head yasterday in work. How could werewolves become &quot;sea wolves&quot;? Like, 2,5 meter wolf-man on ship? Or maybe just a old sailor? Maybe pirates? Very light topic for running with your ideas to name character sea wolves. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think that shapechanging on long sea travels could be a real problem...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T21:23:56-07:00","id":144091,"title":"","content":"I dunno, doesn't seem all that problematic. Sure going Gauru is dumb, but is it that much worse to do it on a boat than it is to do it in a small town of 500-1000 people?<br /> <br /> I like the idea of a pack of wolf pirates or coast guard or something. Plus &quot;Death Rage on a Boat&quot; sounds like a great horror movie. <i>So good</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T22:29:09-07:00","id":144180,"title":"","content":"There's a Storm Lord lodge for that sort of thing in Lodges: the Faithful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T22:34:24-07:00","id":144192,"title":"","content":"Was just about to mention that. Lodge of the Maelstrom I believe it is. Their sigil is Mjolnir with the Storm Lord eye. <br /> <br /> They protect the land from threats from the ocean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T23:05:49-07:00","id":144205,"title":"","content":"Gotta travel somehow. Providing you avoided dipping into kuruth you'd be okay. The sea can be pretty calming, and I could see entire ships of wolves and wolf-blooded easily making large tracts of it their territory. Were they in your pack, you likely wouldn't even need to worry about not shapeshifting in front of them. Even if you were with a crew of regular sailors, you'd just avoid it for a while. Maybe take the night watch and stretch for a bit but otherwise stay in human form.<br /> <br /> There's not much in the World of Darkness about marine stuff, the werewolf stuff that goes into it suggests there's something big and scary in the ocean. And old.<br /> <br /> There's a Bizarro anthology called Cripple Wolf, one of the stories is about a disabled veteran who's also a werewolf (of the turn on the full moon and kill everyone variety) and happens to be on an airplane when the story occurs. If you were one of the black-out-and-kill-everything werewolves, yes, travel would be hard. Fortunately Forsaken avoids that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T00:58:02-07:00","id":144243,"title":"","content":"Too lazy to go and look up the rules for drowning. Would Gauru just let you tank drowning damage? If so, could just pitch someone in Kuruth overboard and drop anchor after a minute of floating away from them. :P No contagion risk. No meaningful collateral damage risk. Just the minor challenge of the grab-and-toss and then wait for them to swim back after cooling off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T02:11:23-07:00","id":144309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/144079-sea-wolves?p=144243#post144243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Too lazy to go and look up the rules for drowning. Would Gauru just let you tank drowning damage? If so, could just pitch someone in Kuruth overboard and drop anchor after a minute of floating away from them. :P No contagion risk. No meaningful collateral damage risk. Just the minor challenge of the grab-and-toss and then wait for them to swim back after cooling off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Drowning: You take bashing every turn up to your Stamina, which you can't regenerate until you breathe again, after the Stamina threshold, it's lethal, IIRC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T05:18:20-07:00","id":144370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/144079-sea-wolves?p=144205#post144205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's not much in the World of Darkness about marine stuff, the werewolf stuff that goes into it suggests there's something big and scary in the ocean. And old.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, <i>War Against the Pure</i> suggests that the ocean is ruled by a goddess who is capricious as Luna herself. As for sea wolves, I had one idea:<br /> <br /> Viking raider werewolves. They keep a base in Iceland and down to the Faroe Islands, and spend their time between the Shadow on those flecks of land and kicking butt on the great blue sea. I want to see one call a shark totem up to leap from the ocean and tear into a boat like Jaws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T07:00:43-07:00","id":144443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/144079-sea-wolves?p=144370#post144370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, <i>War Against the Pure</i> suggests that the ocean is ruled by a goddess who is capricious as Luna herself. As for sea wolves, I had one idea:<br /> <br /> Viking raider werewolves. They keep a base in Iceland and down to the Faroe Islands, and spend their time between the Shadow on those flecks of land and kicking butt on the great blue sea. I want to see one call a shark totem up to leap from the ocean and tear into a boat like Jaws.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohhh no. Yep. Yeah, I just imagined Calypso from <i>Pirates of the Caribbean </i>but in a werewolf game. And it's an awesome idea (now I wanna do a <i>Werewolf Pirates of the Caribbean</i> game).<br /> <br /> I had a Mummy Storyteller character who was a viking raider captain, the cult was his crew and they terrorized the Baltic Sea. Then the ship gets sunk while he's asleep and he doesn't wake up until the modern Sothic Turn. Great way to explain a lack of Cult, Relics, and Tomb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T11:25:33-07:00","id":144649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/144079-sea-wolves?p=144443#post144443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ohhh no. Yep. Yeah, I just imagined Calypso from <i>Pirates of the Caribbean </i>but in a werewolf game. And it's an awesome idea (now I wanna do a <i>Werewolf Pirates of the Caribbean</i> game).<br /> <br /> I had a Mummy Storyteller character who was a viking raider captain, the cult was his crew and they terrorized the Baltic Sea. Then the ship gets sunk while he's asleep and he doesn't wake up until the modern Sothic Turn. Great way to explain a lack of Cult, Relics, and Tomb.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not have him team up with a bunch of Blood Talons who are waging a war against English Storm Lords who are trying to halt the Danish invasion of England?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T13:15:28-07:00","id":144778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_contain