of the sea in some Mermaid-like spirit Underwater Kingdom.<br /> <br /> Or you can take the whole ship into the Shadow. That would allow for some awesome Flying Dutchman scenes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1261-doc-lumbago","name":"Doc Lumbago","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T14:10:27-07:00","id":144841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doc Lumbago</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/144079-sea-wolves?p=144791#post144791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you enter the Shadow in the middle of the Ocean ? Yes, you can of course but do you need to swim?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Moreso than usual.</i> The Shadow of the ocean is shaped by the memories and perceptions of the creatures that inhabit it.<br /> <br /> I strongly suspect that without knowing the currents and arcane shortcuts Mother Ocean's body is essentially <i>bounded infinity</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theo